# Line endings are normalised to LF inside the repository; git hands out
# whatever the platform wants on checkout. Without this, committing from
# Windows warns about CRLF conversion on every touched file, and a clone on
# another platform sees the whole tree as modified before anyone edits it.
* text=auto

# Committed binaries git must not interpret. The music is raw PCM: a
# line-ending "fix" would corrupt it, and audio corruption is the kind that
# shows up as a click nobody can place rather than as an error.
*.wav   binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary

# Replay recordings (netplay/replay.hpp) are packed little-endian structs.
# Nothing commits them today, but a desync report is exactly the sort of
# attachment that ends up in a repo one day.
*.bsdr  binary
